      "ChannelTitle": "Kanishk Nishar",
      "Description": "(Timings below.) Recorded live at Severance Hall in Cleveland on 7 May 1970. The broadcast begins with words from Szell about the shootings at Kent State University in Ohio earlier in the week. The concert contained Weber\u0027s overture to \u0027Oberon\u0027 [then Mozart\u0027s 40th, K550, not in this video] and the Beethoven. It was Szell\u0027s last performance of the Eroica in Cleveland, before the tour of Japan and Korea and his final concert in Anchorage which included the Eroica. According to Michael Charry\u0027s biography, after the 7 May concert Szell \u0022allowed himself a rare bit of self-praise, saying \u0027Now THAT was a performance!\u0027 \u0022 (Charry p.284)\n\n00:00 Szell\u0027s speech\n01:35 Oberon overture\n12:03 Beethoven 3:i Allegro con brio\n28:05 Beethoven 3:ii Marcia funebre, Adagio assai\n45:25 Beethoven 3:iii Scherzo, Allegro vivace - trio\n51:50 Beethoven 3:iv Finale, Allegro molto, poco andante",
